{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 40,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speak ye comfortably to Jerusalem, and cry to her, that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned: for she hath received from the LORD'S hand double for all her sins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the LORD, make straight in the desert a highway for our God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every valley shall be exalted, and every mountain and hill shall be made low: and the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough places plain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the glory of the LORD shall be revealed, and all flesh together shall see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice said, Cry. And he said, What shall I cry? All flesh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grass, and all its goodliness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the flower of the field:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: because the spirit of the LORD bloweth upon it: surely the people ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall shall stand forever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Zion, that bringest good tidings, go up upon the high mountain: O Jerusalem, that bringest good tidings, lift up thy voice with strength; lift ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " up, be not afraid; say to the cities of Judah, Behold your God!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the LORD GOD will come with strong ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hand",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and his arm will rule for him: behold, his reward ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him, and his work before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will feed his flock like a shepherd: he will gather the lambs with his arm, and carry ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his bosom, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will gently lead those that are with young.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, and measured heaven with the span, and comprehended the dust of the earth in a measure, and weighed the mountains in scales, and the hills in a balance?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath directed the Spirit of the LORD, or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his counselor hath taught him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With whom took he counsel, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " instructed him, and taught him in the path of judgment, and taught him knowledge, and showed to him the way of understanding?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the nations ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a drop of a bucket, and are counted as the small dust of the balance: behold, he taketh up the isles as a very little thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Lebanon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not sufficient to burn, nor the beasts of it sufficient for a burnt-offering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All nations before him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as nothing; and they are counted to him less than nothing, and vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom then will ye liken God? or what likeness will ye compare to him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The workman melteth a graven image, and the goldsmith spreadeth it over with gold, and casteth silver chains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so impoverished that he hath no oblation chooseth a tree ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will not rot; he seeketh for himself a skillful workman to prepare a graven image ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall not be moved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have ye not known? have ye not heard? hath it not been told you from the beginning? have ye not understood from the foundations of the earth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth, and its inhabitants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as grasshoppers; that stretcheth out the heavens as a curtain, and spreadeth them out as a tent to dwell in:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That bringeth the princes to nothing; he maketh the judges of the earth as vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, they shall not be planted; yes, they shall not be sown: yes, their stock shall not take root in the earth: and he shall also blow upon them, and they shall wither, and the whirlwind shall take them away as stubble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom then will ye liken me, or shall I be equaled? saith the Holy One.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up your eyes on high, and behold who hath created these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names, by the greatness of his might, for that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is strong in power; not one faileth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and speakest, O Israel, My way is hid from the LORD, and my judgment is passed over by my God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no searching of his understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He giveth power to the faint; and to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no might he increaseth strength.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fall:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.40.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.40.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; they shall walk, and not faint.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
